      "raw_text": "To find the percentage of all puppies that have spots, we need to follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of puppies.**\nJennifer has 8 puppies.\nBrandon has 12 puppies.\nTotal puppies = $8 + 12 = 20$.\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the total number of spotted puppies.**\nJennifer has 3 spotted puppies.\nBrandon has 4 spotted puppies.\nTotal spotted puppies = $3 + 4 = 7$.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the percentage of spotted puppies.**\nThe formula for percentage is:\n$$ \\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Part}}{\\text{Whole}} \\right) \\times 100 $$\n\nSubstitute the values we found:\n$$ \\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{7}{20} \\right) \\times 100 $$\n\nFirst, divide 7 by 20:\n$$ \\frac{7}{20} = 0.35 $$\n\nThen, multiply by 100 to get the percentage:\n$$ 0.35 \\times 100 = 35\\% $$\n\n#### 35%<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To find the percentage of all puppies that have spots, we need to follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of puppies.**\nJennifer has 8 puppies.\nBrandon has 12 puppies.\nTotal puppies = $8 + 12 = 20$.\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the total number of spotted puppies.**\nJennifer has 3 spotted puppies.\nBrandon has 4 spotted puppies.\nTotal spotted puppies = $3 + 4 = 7$.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the percentage of spotted puppies.**\nThe formula for percentage is:\n$$ \\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Part}}{\\text{Whole}} \\right) \\times 100 $$\n\nSubstitute the values we found:\n$$ \\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{7}{20} \\right) \\times 100 $$\n\nFirst, divide 7 by 20:\n$$ \\frac{7}{20} = 0.35 $$\n\nThen, multiply by 100 to get the percentage:\n$$ 0.35 \\times 100 = 35\\% $$\n\n#### 35%",
